  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1155 PM CDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nMonday brings a pattern shift as a large scale low pressure \nsystem over the western CONUS moves east flattening out and \npushing eastward the high pressure system over southeastern CONUS.\nThis will allow for moisture to return to the region in force \nstarting later on Monday. The arrival of the moisture coupled with\nthe dynamics of the weather system will allow for a low chance for\nafternoon to evening rain showers and thunderstorms. Tuesday is\nshaping up to be the most active day as even more moisture and a\ncold front arrives in the panhandles. This will bring a medium to\nhigh chance for rain showers and thunderstorms favoring more of\nthe northwestern panhandles. Moisture continues to stream across\nthe panhandles through the rest of the work week. This will allow\nfor a low to medium chance for further rain showers and\nthunderstorms through Friday. All this active weather will most\nlikely lead to cooler conditions for the panhandles for the\npanhandles starting on Tuesday.",
